values ('d1e2f3a4-5b6c-4e31-8f01-2a3b4c5d6e11', 'constitutional-law-civil-liberties', 'Constitutional Law / Civil Liberties', 'This course studies American constitutional rights and civil liberties through Supreme Court doctrine, constitutional text, historical development, litigation strategy, and contemporary public-law disputes. Students examine due process, equal protection, speech, press, religion, criminal procedure, privacy, voting, state action, incorporation, federalism, remedies, and current civil-liberties conflicts involving technology, education, national security, public health, and democracy.');

